# contents — what a container holds is unknown, and the observing mind chooses which it looks at
#
# Observing a container discloses how many things it holds and nothing else: one anonymous symbol
# each, joined on one row under it. A click on any of them asks a mind to look at SOMETHING it
# holds, and the mind chooses which — exactly as with the things of a kind on a card. A thing is
# named by being looked at, never before. A script may still name one (that pins the observation
# to it); naming the holder leaves the choice to the mind, which is what a player's click does.
#
# Played in the childhood, whose "myself" holds the fragments of the memory at hand as a chest holds
# what is in it: the one container a script reaches with no preparation. --seed 42 fixes both the
# memory and what the playground's mind picks.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode ChildhoodReminescence 60
advance 12 180

click observe person
choose childhood_reminescence
advance 12 180

# --- six things held, none of them named on the screen ---
expect-state symbols click observe "a scream" in "Myself"
expect-state symbols click observe "a whisper" in "Myself"
point observe Myself
wait
expect-state pointer-label ground=yellow text=observe · a memory
expect-no-state trees element "a

# --- asked for something it holds, the mind chooses which ---
click observe Myself
choose childhood_reminescence
advance 12 180
# (at this seed the playground's mind takes the laugh)
expect-state trees element "a laugh"
expect-no-state symbols click observe "a laugh"
expect-state symbols click observe "a scream" in "Myself"

# --- a script that names one has made the choice for it ---
click observe "sobs"
choose childhood_reminescence
advance 12 180
expect-state trees element "sobs"
quit
